# DTF tier manifest: debian-virtual-local-members  (artifact-keeper#6548; 1.13.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + client.apt (debian:12).
#
# THE BUG
#   #6548 a Virtual Debian repository whose members are all Local built its
#         Release and Packages from its own artifact rows, of which it has
#         none, so apt saw a valid (and, with a key, signed) empty index.
#         Fixed: a Virtual's index is the union of the Local and Staging
#         members the caller may read, in priority order; a Virtual with no
#         readable member answers 404 instead of an empty index.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   Two .debs built by the real dpkg-deb in the Debian client, one uploaded to
#   each of two public Local repositories (native pool PUT). A public Virtual
#   lists both. apt reads it with [trusted=yes]: signing is not what broke.
#
# THE GATES
#   (CONTROL) both images: each member's own Packages lists its package.
#   (FIX)     the Virtual's Packages lists both packages and its Release
#             vouches for that exact index (sha256 and size); a real apt-get
#             update + install through the Virtual installs the second
#             member's package; a Virtual with no members answers 404 on
#             Packages (red on main: an empty 200 index, apt finds nothing).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem client.apt"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
COVERS="6548"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
